  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Women-Led Silk Production and Innovation at Bere Sericulture Production PLC&quot;</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The enterprise is primarily producing silk cocoon thread for companies exporting finished silk fabrics. They are sourced raw materials from its own 8 -hectare mulberry and castor plantation as well as from over 200 trained women out -growers. Key operational challenges include limited technical capacity among out -grower women, reduced feed quality and fungal infections in mulberry plants, Inefficiencies in cocoon yield. Quality and design limitations in finished silk products. To address these, the enterprise plans to strengthen silkworm rearing practices through inspections, plant and silkworm diagnostics, and a silkworm seed centre. Improve design and product quality by training staff and recruiting skilled designers and garment experts.</narrative>
  </description>
